Let $V = \bigoplus_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} V_{(n)}$ be a simple vertex operator algebra over $\mathbb{C}$ satisfying:
(i) $V_{(0)} = \mathbb{C}\mathbf{1}$ and $V_{(n)} = 0$ for $n < 0$;
(ii) $V$ is $C_2$-cofinite, i.e., $\dim V/C_2(V) < \infty$, where $C_2(V) = \mathrm{span}\{u_{-2}v : u,v \in V\}$;
(iii) the contragredient module $V'$ is isomorphic to $V$ as a $V$-module;
(iv) every grading-restricted generalized $V$-module is completely reducible.

Let $G$ be a finite group of automorphisms of $V$. For each $g \in G$, let $\mathcal{C}_g$ denote the category of grading-restricted generalized $g$-twisted $V$-modules, and let
$$\mathcal{C} = \bigoplus_{g \in G} \mathcal{C}_g.$$

Recall that a $G$-crossed (braided) tensor category in the sense of Turaev is a tensor category $\mathcal{C}$ equipped with a decomposition $\mathcal{C} = \bigoplus_{g \in G}\mathcal{C}_g$, a monoidal $G$-action $\varphi: G \to \mathrm{Aut}_\otimes(\mathcal{C})$ such that $\varphi_h(\mathcal{C}_g) \subseteq \mathcal{C}_{hgh^{-1}}$, tensor products satisfying $\mathcal{C}_g \otimes \mathcal{C}_h \subseteq \mathcal{C}_{gh}$, and a $G$-braiding $c_{X,Y}: X \otimes Y \to \varphi_g(Y) \otimes X$ for $X \in \mathcal{C}_g$ satisfying the appropriate hexagon axioms.

Question: Does $\mathcal{C} = \bigoplus_{g \in G}\mathcal{C}_g$ carry the structure of a $G$-crossed (braided) tensor category in the sense of Turaev?

